# Testcontainers builds this Dockerfile with the solution root as its context, but it looks for the
# ignore file next to the Dockerfile (<dockerfile>.dockerignore, falling back to .dockerignore in
# the same directory) and never reads the context root's .dockerignore. Without this file the host's
# bin/ and obj/ are tarred into the build context, and obj/ records absolute host paths -- the ANTLR
# sources LibAlpmSharp generates among them -- so `dotnet build` inside the image fails with
# CS2001 "Source file ... could not be found". Keep this in step with the root .dockerignore.
#
# BuildKit also prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the context root's file, so `docker build`
# and Testcontainers now exclude exactly the same things.
**/.dockerignore
**/.env
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/azds.yaml
**/bin
**/charts
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
LICENSE
README.md
